From: thiswillbeyourgithub
 <26625900+thiswillbeyourgithub@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:21:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] voxtral-tts: dump stage-0 codes per request, on request

The open checkpoint ships no audio encoder, so the only source of real
audio/codes pairs to train one on is this model generating them: stage 0 IS
the text -> on-manifold-codes map, and what it emits here is exactly the
table-space ids a voice prefix carries, so a dump is usable as a voice with
no conversion.

A request sets voxtral_dump_codes in extra_params and the frames are appended
to <VOXTRAL_CODE_DUMP_DIR>/<tag>.i16 as raw int16 rows. The tag rides the same
per-row sampling_extra_args route as the noise seed, so it is per request and
stays correct under concurrency; appending is the only format that survives a
request being preempted or cancelled mid-utterance. Nothing is written, and
the env var need not exist, unless a request asks.
